WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Enter the customer price before tax: $1,000.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Enter $600 for labour and materials. The proposed discount is zero.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Subtract $600 in direct costs from $1,000 in price. That leaves $400 before overhead.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Divide $400 of gross profit by the $1,000 customer price. Forty cents of each sales dollar remains after direct costs.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Divide the same $400 of gross profit by the $600 direct cost. The smaller starting number gives the larger percentage.

